.claude/agents/lattice-implementer.md:243:Always read the canonical reports `acceptance_topology_check`, `pre_review_check_read`, `acceptance_rollout_report_read`, and `acceptance_rollout_check`, and report their status honestly. Missing or non-PASS signed per-Story evidence is a blocker only when a canonical report says `blocking=true`, the project mode is `enforce`, or the work makes an explicit promotion claim. In `observe` or `warn`, `legacy_missing` or `partial` is advisory only: never fabricate a topology and never upgrade it to a formal pass. A report that claims PASS or promotion still requires a current signed receipt and exact full 3 rounds × 2 hosts (`codex-cli` + `claude-cli`); reject degraded 3x1. Prompt prose is never gate evidence. Rollback may only change the configured mode and must preserve every report, receipt, diagnostic, and prior evidence.
